.TH NET 1 "September 2026" "Peios netd 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
net \- inspect and control the Peios network manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B net status
.br
.B net renew
.I interface
.br
.B net reconcile
.br
.B net rules
.br
.B net profiles
.br
.B net wait
.I level
.RI [ timeout-seconds ]
.br
.B net version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B net
is the stateless operator client for
.BR netd (8).
Network configuration remains in the registry below
.BR Machine\\System\\Network ;
this command observes the effective state and asks the daemon to perform
bounded control operations.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show machine readiness and each interface's policy verdict, link state,
addresses, routes, name servers, network identity, and lease state.
.TP
.BI renew " interface"
Renew the named interface's offered-address lease. This operation requires
the NETWORK_CONTROL right on the netd control object.
.TP
.B reconcile
Ask netd to compare the kernel with the current registry state immediately.
This operation requires NETWORK_CONTROL.
.TP
.B rules
List the interface-layer policy forest from the registry.
.TP
.B profiles
List network profiles and the values each profile defines directly.
.TP
.BI wait " level " "[timeout-seconds]"
Wait until machine readiness reaches
.BR link ,
.BR addressed ,
or
.BR routed .
The default timeout is 60 seconds.
.TP
.B version
Print the client version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/netd/control.sock
The native netd control object.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success, one on an operational failure or timeout, and two for invalid
command syntax.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR netd (8),
.BR reg (1),
.BR regman (1)
